# End-user copy

Internal, techy copy is NEVER shown to an end user.

Labels, hints, info panels, empty states, buttons, and errors say what the person can do or what will happen. They do not mention how a list was saved, which API answered, snapshot rules, table names, or why a list was built.

Bad: `X tokens, plus tokens with over $100 of XPR in an Alcor pool. That list is saved.`

Good: `Holders of this token receive the drop.`

Skill: `.cursor/skills/user-facing-copy/SKILL.md`.
